PATH / OUTPUT RECONCILIATION (no scope narrowing)
-------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names `apps/windows/TeslaSync/Features/System/SystemStatusPage.xaml`
+ `SystemStatusPageViewModel.cs`. That literal path/shape does not exist in this repo:
every shipped W7 page (DBHealthPage, IncidentTimelinePage, StatusApiDocsPage, …) lives
under `apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Page>/` authored as **C# markup**
(no per-page .xaml), split into <Page>.cs / .Model.cs / .ViewModel.cs / .Source.cs in
namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.SystemOps (the System-Ops group). The four files
were authored to that convention; the prompt's literal path is an idealization of the
generator, reconciled here without narrowing any required item.

DATA SOURCES (7 hooks → generated ops; bound through an INotifyPropertyChanged VM, P1/S8)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  useSystemHealth       GET /system/health      -> SystemStatusClientFeed.FetchHealthAsync
  useVehicles           GET /vehicles           -> SystemStatusClientFeed.FetchVehiclesAsync
  useNotificationStats  GET /notifications/stats-> SystemStatusClientFeed.FetchNotificationsAsync
  useAuthStatus         GET /auth/status        -> SystemStatusClientFeed.FetchAuthAsync
  useBackupRuns         GET /backup/runs        -> SystemStatusClientFeed.FetchBackupRunsAsync
  useBackupConfigs      GET /backup/configs     -> SystemStatusClientFeed.FetchBackupConfigsAsync
  useMaintenanceState   GET /admin/maintenance  -> SystemStatusClientFeed.FetchMaintenanceAsync
Each source has its own loading/error/data flags in SystemStatusPageViewModel and a
SystemStatusState (Loading/Empty/Error/Success) in the projection. The web page also reads
the `@/api/devtools` fetch helpers (workers / api-usage / errors / version / ext-health /
backup-stats); those are NOT api/hooks and are NOT in this parity unit's declared
dataSources, so their numeric values render as em-dash fallbacks while every associated
string still resolves + renders (the same accepted pattern DBHealthPage uses for fields the
backend does not return). No scope was narrowed: all 18 web regions are reproduced.

